{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJqQPTujY21FK1zYgZK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night: `launchctl print` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`. It fails and then can't report the failure, because three bugs are stacked:\n\n1. **`claude` isn't logged in under launchd.** The error log shows \"Not logged in\" every night. The plist only set `PATH`, so `USER` was missing and the CLI couldn't find its login in the keychain.\n2. **`status=$?` kills the script.** In zsh, `status` is a read-only variable, so assigning to it ends the script right before it would send the failure note. This is why you got no failure notes either.\n3. **`notify.sh` would have failed at night anyway.** It gets the bot token from the keychain, which is locked at 02:30 on that box. `config.toml` was there as a fallback, but nothing ever read it.\n\n**Fixes (explained in `ANSWER.md`):**\n- **plist:** added `USER`, `HOME` and `~/.local/bin` to the environment.\n- **Script:** renamed `status` to `rc`, and the prompt now goes in on stdin. The `.err` log now gets each run's start time, exit code and duration. An empty output file counts as a failure, and a failed notification is logged.\n- **`notify.sh`:** looks for the token in `TG_BOT_TOKEN`, then the keychain, then `config.toml`, and logs an error if none has one. `curl -f` makes Telegram errors fail instead of passing as success.\n- **`config.toml`:** now readable only by you (`chmod 600`).\n\n**What I checked:** the plist passes `plutil -lint`, both scripts pass a syntax check, and the token comes out of `config.toml` correctly. I didn't run the job: that needs your Mac, and sending a Telegram message would break the no-external-services rule. `ANSWER.md` has the commands to reload and run it once, and how to confirm both the success and the failure messages arrive. If `claude` still says \"Not logged in\" after the change, the fallback is `claude setup-token`; the steps are there too.\n\n**Two other things:**\n- Your `README.md` has a Telegram bot token in plain text, different from the one in `config.toml`. You should remove it, and probably revoke it.\n- worklore suggested a story describing this exact failure (\"zsh killed the messenger\"), and I used it. I didn't report back to worklore that it worked, since that would mean sending something to an external service."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1666,"cache_read_input_tokens":29709,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1666},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58735416-60fc-420a-a6af-daf98c025dc9","uuid":"b4cb7343-bfc9-4e1f-ac2a-4813236ce410","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:25:19.830Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJqQ9LTnbbid4MRBu2A"}
